# Generated builds, fetched dependencies, reports and distribution staging.
# Includes minimal Ubuntu inputs in .tools/headless and server packages/evidence in out/.
# Graphics/DXC/validation source caches stay in .tools/graphics; generated SPIR-V,
# binary readbacks, validation layers and reports use build/ and out/graphics*/.
# Standalone graphics probe packages and relocation receipts also belong in out/ or dist/.
# Device/presentation JSONL traces, local verification helpers and receipts stay in out/.
# Stress/resource traces and Runtime relocation packages also stay in out/ or dist/.
# Offline shader generations, dependency manifests and build receipts stay in out/.
# GPU resource readbacks and offscreen qualification traces also stay in out/.
# Window cube captures and packaged .sharkshader bundles stay in build/, out/ or dist/.
# Keep shaders/ source recipes and HLSL fixtures eligible for versioning.
# Keep generated agent/session reports under out/; public schemas/examples stay tracked.
# EnTT/GLM caches and scene/schema/query qualification reports stay under out/ or build/.
# TLS source caches, generated local identities and network receipts stay under out/ or build/.
# Explicitly public test-only certificates in tests/fixtures/network remain versioned.
# Session enrollment experiments, local credentials and process receipts stay under out/.
# Replication traces, raw payload diagnostics and local multi-process receipts use out/ or build/.
# Interest budgets, shaped relay barriers and per-connection traces use out/ or build/.
# Adversity relays, PID/barrier files and process resource samples use out/ or build/.
# Source JSON dependency caches and codec qualification output use out/ or build/.
# Scene activation/capture qualification and temporary snapshots use out/ or build/.
# Project file conflict/interruption fixtures and receipts use out/ or build/.
# Integrated persistence qualification, migrations and recovery receipts use out/ or build/.
# Live database files, rollback journals, SQLite caches and recovery receipts use out/ or build/.
# Durable character/session restart fixtures and roster/save receipts also use out/ or build/.
# Economic transaction databases, operation receipts and process barriers use out/ or build/.
# Runtime recovery journals, worker barriers and I/O-fault receipts use out/ or build/.
# Database upgrade backups, isolated restore candidates and migration receipts use out/ or build/.
# Connected durable qualification databases, child traces and restore receipts use out/ or build/.
# Authoring-command, atomic-preview and shared-history snapshots/receipts use out/ or build/.
# Retained-retry/lost-reply intents and restart receipts also use out/ or build/.
# Connected authoring qualification projects and publication-fault receipts use out/ or build/.
# FeatureWorld run results and temporary persistence projects use out/ or build/.
# Integrated coverage audits and embedded assertion-failure receipts use out/ or build/.
# Asset catalog snapshots, sidecar fault fixtures and qualification receipts use out/ or build/.
# Background asset-job traces and bounded worker test receipts use out/ or build/.
# Keep authored .sharkasset metadata, asset fixtures and public identity contracts versioned.
# Supervised CPU/GPU execution receipts, native readbacks and token evidence use out/ or build/.
# Keep assets/FeatureWorld source project/scene, native cases and coverage documentation versioned.
# Storage inventories, cleanup receipts and verified evidence archives also stay in out/.
# Keep tools/archive_evidence.py and its tests eligible for versioning.
# Keep independently authored database fixtures and storage documentation eligible for versioning.
# Authored .sharkproject/.sharkscene fixtures and format documentation stay versioned.
